{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792601016,"nonce":"ZfwzCuXJu5fl8KgfD01gSCmeZGI=","message":"Implemented owned, bounded snapshot preparation in zyntax_embed. SnapshotPreparation permits one worker per process, rejects additional jobs rather than queuing, checks cancellation between optimizer passes and writes, validates sources/resolution again before atomic publication, and detaches without joining on Drop. Explicit finish is available for host prewarming. Worker inputs contain owned HIR/body-free metadata, never runtime/plugin pointers. Lowering is performed once; encoding borrows the retained representation. Small closed graphs finish optimization inline to avoid leaving short-process warm caches unfinished.\n\nTS execution uses closed-root cache keys (including sorted explicit roots), preserves separate reusable open snapshots, and can seed a scoped entry from an open checked artifact. Only reached executable function metadata is retained in closed entries. An immediately usable lowered fallback is persisted before optional background optimization. Raw release summaries avoid requiring unrelated bodies to be decoded; generic templates remain available. Interpreter-first execution, array GEPs, automatic releases and initializer order are preserved. Raw lowered snapshots now reject unrelocatable effects/handlers before encoding. The standalone synchronous/open preparation API remains available.\n\nValidation: full LLVM compiler suite 882 passed, 16 ignored; final TS LLVM/allocation-audit suite 83 passed, 4 diagnostic ignores; final embed lib/initializer/borrowed-body suite 106 passed; default-feature project-cache suite 13 passed. Cached and uncached differential conformance each passed 735 comparisons across interpreter, baseline and LLVM, total 1,470. TS/embed all-target Clippy and compiler lib Clippy passed with warnings denied. Parser-only WASM and Python/Lua/ZynML LLVM library checks passed. Dedicated tests cover runtime drop before worker completion, non-blocking cancellation behind a blocked resolver, occupied worker rejection, changed dependencies, cancelled publication preserving prior bytes, concurrent atomic publishers, root-policy isolation, unavailable persistence, large reached graphs and generic list aliases through actual JIT promotions.\n\nThe newly exercised raw path exposed a list-header returned-alias lifetime defect, fixed separately in ce378309fbee770e93eb4ebc52dab67c2b98bde7 (issue 928a1696d619e11bf2e9da925606c0161e399da84306ad31e562cd780d903cc7). The separate global runtime callback isolation issue 718284cd3fe83b90248bf068576db3f97cb48dceacb33ca5c0ef2cd999cb18ec remains open; runtime-owning test fixtures are serialized.\n\nExact-source NUC comparison against the prior synchronous HIR cache (not the older AST-only cache): i5-1250P, Rust 1.101.0-nightly c36f14571, LLVM 21.1.8, identical lock/profile/features. Nine fresh cold stores per fixture/mode plus nine shuffled warm samples per fixture/mode, 162 measured child processes. LLVM selected, baseline threshold 2,000,000,000, OSR disabled: this isolates interpreter-first startup, not tier throughput. All stdout/status checks passed. Frozen binaries, CPUs 0-7; no Cargo between runs. Pre-sample checks observed zero build jobs, \u003c=0.670 busy cores, \u003c=70C, stable binary hashes. These checks were pre-sample, not continuous monitoring. Local timings were excluded because unrelated Cargo jobs were active.\n\nMedian process wall ms, previous -\u003e candidate:\n- tiny: cold 5.079 -\u003e 5.748; warm HIR 4.740 -\u003e 5.325; uncached 4.920 -\u003e 5.637.\n- wide 1,000-function fixture: cold 89.506 -\u003e 17.984; warm HIR 8.299 -\u003e 5.623; uncached 16.683 -\u003e 16.759.\n- 24-library imports: cold 12.898 -\u003e 12.952; warm HIR 5.907 -\u003e 6.714; uncached 9.321 -\u003e 10.129.\nCold child CPU ms previous -\u003e candidate: tiny 5.313 -\u003e 5.930; wide 89.802 -\u003e 18.068; imports 12.873 -\u003e 13.026. Snapshot bytes previous -\u003e candidate: tiny 6549 -\u003e 6560; wide 1465128 -\u003e 145093; imports 225241 -\u003e 225253.\n\nThe wide cold gain is about 4.98x, warm about 1.48x, primarily from selective lowering/metadata. These small graphs finish inline, so the measurements do not establish a worker-throughput improvement. Worker lifetime/cancellation is established by deterministic tests and a \u003e128-reached-function regression. An initial worker-only policy regressed warm imports to about 8.1 ms versus 6.2 ms; recording raw summaries alone did not recover it, motivating bounded inline completion. Final small scripts still incur roughly 0.6-0.8 ms overhead, including the uncached controls. Track phase-level investigation separately in bbb12fa75ae0ba87b2c0d0f371b92c45712c3d781a84308f77bc073e08160b3d; do not attribute it solely to snapshots or claim an across-the-board startup win.\n\nAuthoritative report: /private/tmp/ts-background-nuc-verified.json and /home/raikage/zyntax-ts-background-nuc-verified.json. Candidate /home/raikage/zyntax-ts-background-zynode-verified SHA256 d54ac83bf673726c787a1e1e07a1301c9bba82e045e4fa9235da7a83c435497d. Previous /home/raikage/zyntax-ts-cache-zynode-final SHA256 b53bca21e9cb1241f687756d076b6f1d996c7ee45681328866da15932e3226a4. Logs: /private/tmp/ts-background-{full,ts-final,embed-verified,default,clippy-final,compiler-clippy,wasm,frontends}.log and conformance{,-cached}.json.\n\nPython and Lua can reuse this shared worker/compiler/publication path. Their CLIs still need source/import/ABI validation and user-project cache integration; their builtins are already prelowered. No Python/Lua timings or hot-loop performance claims are made here. Parent 0c26889a7cd2c4060eb94ef93fd808c2857089dbf714735ca52b5d071bdb1564 remains open for further module coverage.","files":null}]}